This product ports ideas, not code, from UniiChat
(https://github.com/VictorTaelin/uniichat), Copyright 2026 Higher Order
Company, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The ideas were
reimplemented in this codebase's own style; no source or text was copied.
What was taken, and from which commit, is tracked in docs/uniichat.md:

- A summary the model refuses, or leaves empty, becomes its source,
  clipped (Memory.ts, Memory.build): SPEC E33.
- Provider keys kept out of the processes the agent runs (Config.ts):
  SPEC E34.
- A WebSocket heartbeat, and a client that drops a silent socket
  (Server.ts, View.ts): SPEC "Protocol".
- A failed model request asked again on `retry-after` and
  `x-should-retry`, and a stream with no bytes for a while cut, with
  UniiChat's idle times (Agent.ts, Anthropic.ts, OpenAI.ts): SPEC E35.
- Subagents with the master's tools on any device, working directly in
  a folder (Agent.ts, Machine.ts): SPEC E36.
- A subagent's report starting a turn of the master (Agent.ts): SPEC E39.
- Subagents going on from their logs after a restart (Agent.ts):
  SPEC E40.
- Each client act kept by the client until answered and sent again on
  the next socket, and done once by the server however often it comes
  (View.ts, Server.ts Chat.apply): SPEC E41.
- No one frame holding the whole history a client lacks: UniiChat sends
  each message or summary in a frame of its own (Server.ts Chat.teach);
  ours pages the snapshot by bytes: SPEC E42.
- A page or client older than the server told to reload, by the wire
  version it connects with (Server.ts): SPEC E44.
- Esc to interrupt a turn, and send as stop with nothing typed (Term.ts,
  web/src/main.ts): SPEC "Web UI".
- A long pasted message folded in the chat (web/src/Html.ts): SPEC
  "Web UI".
- A file edit shown as a diff (Machine.ts): SPEC E45.
